  "$comment": "The words the omnibar's cohort parser understands in English. Data, not code: add phrases here, or per site with the omnibar.phrases config. Comparators use the FHIR search prefixes (lt, le, gt, ge, eq) as their ids: 'under' is lt, 'atMost' le, 'over' gt, 'atLeast' ge, 'aged' eq. Age groups give their source. A word in 'never' can't be a stopword, so text with a negation or an alternative is never read as something else. 'from age' is in both rangeFrom and atLeast on purpose: the reading that covers the most words decides, so 'from age 15 to 49' is a range and 'from age 15' is 15 and over. A site may add phrases in another script; they match only text in that script. The tokenizer drops apostrophes, so 'never' lists contractions without them ('isnt', 'dont').",
